    "rationale": "QUOTE WHAT THE CUSTOMER TYPED. resolve-entity is sent `canonical_code ?? raw` and strips `[-\\s]+` on a product hint, and the CRM lowercases (and sometimes rewrites) its echo, so `resolutions[].token` is routinely not the string the person wrote: here they typed MFG6651-GM and container 1234, and the resolver echoes MFG6651GM and container1234. Both miss renderers - the numbered did-you-mean line and the plain not-found line - map the token back through the node-scope `_rawOfTok` and print the ORIGINAL spelling; the search-scope header on the answer lane shares that one map, so a token can never be spelled two ways in one reply. The type label is prettified on BOTH sources, not just the resolver's: `inbound_shipment` reaches the customer as `(inbound shipment)`, the same vocabulary the media-confirm prefix already prints. `for_raw` in the offer and in dym_last_result_set deliberately stays the RESOLVER token - it is pick-linkage data that output_exchange matches on, not copy - which is why this fixture pins both spellings side by side. KNOWN AND OUT OF SCOPE, pinned as it behaves: `reconcileEntities` joins resolutions to entities with the same broken `norm(token) === norm(raw)` equality, so neither dashed entity is reconciled and both keep the parser's own hint and a null canonical_code. That defect is real and pre-existing (2026-08-22) and was deliberately deferred by the captain; this fixture records it rather than hiding it."
